{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.AJMinimality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJMinimality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.AJTorusAnnihilation"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJMinimality.minimal_order_gt_two_of_noLowOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJMinimality.minimal_order_gt_two_of_noLowOrder","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJMinimality.lean#L168-L183","doc":"**Minimality reduces to `NoLowOrderHomogAnnihilator` (sorry-free logical\nreduction).**  Given the sharp concrete statement `NoLowOrderHomogAnnihilator`\n(no nonzero order-≤2 homogeneous operator annihilates the tower), any\nhomogeneous annihilator with a nonzero coefficient is impossible — i.e. the\nminimal homogeneous annihilation order is `> 2`.  Together with\n`ajHomElement_annihilates` (order-3 annihilation, corpus-proved) and\n`hc3_ne_zero` (order-exactness), this pins the minimal order at exactly 3.\n\nThis lemma REDUCES the [Tr4]-cited `minimality` to the single sharp premise\n`NoLowOrderHomogAnnihilator q` — the smallest honest gap.  That premise is\n**not** provided here: it is the wall (see the audit doc). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJMinimality.figureEight_not_homogAnnihilator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJMinimality.figureEight_not_homogAnnihilator","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJMinimality.lean#L147-L164","doc":"**Order-2 obstruction (sorry-free).**  The order-2 figure-eight coefficient\ntriple `(feCoeff₀, feCoeff₁, feCoeff₂)` is **not** a homogeneous annihilator:\nat any colour `M` where `feRhs q (q^M) ≠ 0` it sends the tower to\n`feRhs ≠ 0`, not `0`.  So the naive order-2 candidate — whose homogenisation\nis `Â_hom` — fails, which is the concrete reason order 3 is forced.  This\nrules out ONE triple; ruling out all of them is `NoLowOrderHomogAnnihilator`\n(the wall). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJMinimality.NoLowOrderHomogAnnihilator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJMinimality.NoLowOrderHomogAnnihilator","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJMinimality.lean#L138-L145","doc":"**Minimality of the order-3 operator among homogeneous annihilators.**  The\nsharp concrete statement that `minimality` reduces to: no *nonzero* order-≤2\nhomogeneous operator annihilates the `4₁` tower.  This is the residual WALL —\nit needs the holonomic-rank / A-polynomial-degree fact absent from Mathlib +\ncorpus.  It is stated here (as the honest reduction target), **never\naxiomatised**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJMinimality.IsHomogAnnihilator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJMinimality.IsHomogAnnihilator","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJMinimality.lean#L132-L136","doc":"An order-≤2 **homogeneous** annihilator of the `4₁` tower: coefficient\nfunctions `c₀,c₁,c₂ : ℤ→K` with\n`c₀(N)·J(N) + c₁(N)·J(N+1) + c₂(N)·J(N+2) = 0` at every colour. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJMinimality.coeffAt_ajHomElement_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJMinimality.coeffAt_ajHomElement_three","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJMinimality.lean#L121-L128","doc":"`hc3` is literally the `L³` coefficient of the torus element `ajHomElement`\n(`coeffAt … 3 = hc3`).  Combined with `hc3_ne_zero`, this witnesses\n`topDeg (ajHomElement q) = 3` at generic `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJMinimality.hc3_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJMinimality.hc3_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJMinimality.lean#L108-L119","doc":"**`Â_hom` is genuinely order 3 — order-exactness (sorry-free).**  Wherever\n`feRhs` and the top figure-eight coefficient `feCoeff₂` are nonzero (the\ngeneric-`q` condition), the `L³` coefficient `hc3` of the homogenised\noperator is nonzero.  So `ajHomElement` is not a disguised order-≤2 operator;\nits `topDeg` is exactly 3, the reference degree the `minimality` field is\nstated against.  This is a NECESSARY ingredient of minimality, not the whole\nof it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.AJMinimality.hc3_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.AJMinimality.hc3_eq","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/AJMinimality.lean#L99-L106","doc":"The `L³` coefficient of the homogenised order-3 operator, evaluated at a\nnonnegative colour, is `−(feRhs·feCoeff₂)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}